OpenScatter is written from scratch. It learns from the behaviour of existing scatters for 3ds Max
as their public documentation describes it; it is not affiliated with their makers and contains
none of their code, names, icons, patterns, distribution maps, presets or assets.

Algorithms

  The blue-noise patterns are built by weighted sample elimination, as described in:
  Cem Yuksel, "Sample Elimination for Generating Poisson Disk Sample Sets", Computer Graphics Forum
  (Proceedings of Eurographics), 2015. The implementation (core/src/pattern.cpp) was written for
  OpenScatter.

  The hash functions (core/include/osc/hash.h) are built on the SplitMix64 finaliser, which its
  author, Sebastiano Vigna, placed in the public domain.

